rmaceuticals, healthcare, automotive, and cleanroom industries. Vestis Corporation was founded in 1936 and is headquartered in Roswell, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Jay Barber Jr. | CEO, President & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $765,337 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 18K people. Revenue per employee of $151K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $318 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $637 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Vestis Corporation is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.9B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -3.3pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $6M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.3pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 466% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.65762323071025},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 175% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Vestis Corporation $VSTS Stock Purchased by Jefferies Financial Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/vestis-corporation-vsts-stock-purchased-by-jefferies-financial-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794480565.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How (VSTS) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.